                <pb facs="0394" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13357: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Swatow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Swatow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-01T22:00:00+08:00">July 1, 1938—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 2—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From 4:30 to 6 p.m., 9 Japanese bombers dropped 71 bombs without warning
                    indiscriminately on various parts of Swatow causing <pb facs="0395" n="391"
                        xml:id="pg391"/> probably 50 deaths among Chinese and unknown number
                    wounded. Father William J. Downs, American of Maryknoll Mission, slightly
                    wounded and his house demolished; no other American casualties.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
